Check service binding, host firewall, cloud security rules, routing, upstream firewalls, and whether the application is listening on the correct interface.

```
ss -lntp
ip route
nft list ruleset
tcpdump -ni any port 443
```

### Advanced

Q8. A server can reach an IP address but cannot resolve domain names. How do you troubleshoot DNS?

```
cat /etc/resolv.conf
resolvectl status
getent hosts example.com
dig example.com
```

Q9. How do you diagnose intermittent packet loss?

```
ping -c 50 target.example.com
mtr -rw target.example.com
ip -s link
```

Correlate the results with interface counters and application metrics; ICMP filtering and rate limiting can distort the results.

### Expert

Q10. A server can establish TCP connections, but users experience intermittent timeouts. How do you investigate?

Examine retransmissions, connection state, MTU, DNS delays, firewall state, upstream load balancers, packet captures, and application response times.

```
ss -s
ss -ti
ip -s link
tcpdump -ni any host 192.0.2.10
```
Replace the documentation IP with the real target address

